*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ---- Project Brain runtime scratch (specs are tracked, scratch is not) ----
.kilo/ecc/project-brain/*.tmp
.kilo/ecc/project-brain/*.append.tmp
  
# ---- Driver-pinning probe modules (evidence input, not product code) ----
# EV-060 established which PostgreSQL drivers satisfy scripts/verify_toolchain.py by building
# each candidate in a throwaway module and running the real gate against it. Those modules are
# inputs to that measurement rather than anything the build compiles: each has its own go.mod
# with a deliberately unpinned or pseudo-versioned require, so including one in the workspace
# would be an attempt to admit exactly what the gate exists to refuse. Kept on disk so
# scripts/probe_driver_pinning.py can re-verify EV-060 rather than trusting the record.
_driver_probe/

# ---- Go workspace module list (CI working-directory artifact, not an input) ----
# Every Go job resolves the workspace with `go work edit -json` into modules.txt in the
# checkout root and then iterates it, and the vulnerability scan refuses to report a clean
# result unless that file exists and is non-empty. Those two properties together mean a
# COMMITTED modules.txt is worse than no file at all: the guard tests for presence and size,
# never for freshness, so a stale tracked copy would let a job whose resolve step failed
# quietly scan a module list from whenever it was last written. Each job must resolve its own.
modules.txt
